Changes to ALEX (microsoft/ALEX @ 4370da6) used by learned-index-mako.

1. ALEX_TRACK_LOOKUP_STATS: lookups update per-node statistics, which makes concurrent
   lookups a data race even under a shared lock. Defining ALEX_TRACK_LOOKUP_STATS=0
   compiles those updates out. The default (1) keeps ALEX's behaviour.
2. Bounds check in AlexDataNode::get_next_filled_position(): find_lower() and find_upper()
   can pass pos == data_capacity_, which read one bitmap word past the end of the array.
   Found by the randomized test in tests/alex_index_test.cc under ThreadSanitizer.
3. Alex::delete_node() downcast each node after destroying it, which is undefined
   behaviour (reported by UBSan). It now casts once, before destroying.
4. extract_rightmost_one() negated the bitmap word as int64_t, which overflows when only
   the top bit is set (reported by UBSan). It now negates as uint64_t; the result is the
   same bit pattern.

